-- title:
--   Birkhoff's far family: behaviour at the first bad parameter
-- statement:
--   Fix $0<\mu<1$ and a Jacobi energy $-c$ below the first critical value. Let $\Sigma_{\mu,c}$ be the selected Levi-Civita component and $\varphi$ a continuous flow on it generated by the Hamiltonian vector field of $K_{\mu,c}$. Let $N(r)$ and $F(r)$ be the perpendicular near and far starts, and $(\sigma,\eta)$ the shooting coordinates (velocity sine and depth). For a near arc of length $\tau$ the crossing state is $\varphi_{-\tau}s$; for a far arc it is $\varphi_\tau s$.
--
--   **End of the far family.** Let $b>0$. Suppose that $F(r)$ admits a far shooting arc for every $0<r<b$, but $F(b)$ does not. Then the crossing coordinates of the far arcs from $F(r)$ converge, as $r\to b^-$, to a point $E$ of the boundary of the rectangle $[-1,1]\times[0,1]$. Moreover, either
--   $$
--   E_1=\pm1\ \text{and}\ E_2>0,\qquad\text{or}\qquad E_2=0\ \text{and}\ E_1>\tfrac{\sqrt2}{2}.
--   $$
--
--   The first case is a tangency with the vertical line; the second is a collision whose arrival direction lies beyond the diagonal. Excluding an interior loss of monotonicity, and an earlier return to the axis, uses Birkhoff's angular-momentum identity (59) on the far side, where the torque about the primary has a definite sign.
-- source:
--   Liu--Salomao, Finite energy foliations in the restricted three-body problem, https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.17867v2, Section 5, proof of Theorem 5.1 (pp. 30-31): the curves Gamma_1, Gamma_2, their continuity and endpoints; after G. D. Birkhoff, The restricted problem of three bodies, Rend. Circ. Mat. Palermo 39 (1915), Sections 16-18 (Collected Mathematical Papers Vol. 1, pp. 731-741).

import Definitions.Def_BirkhoffShootingArcs

namespace BirkhoffGlobalSection

theorem birkhoff_far_arc_end (μ c : ℝ)
    (hμ0 : 0 < μ) (hμ1 : μ < 1)
    (hc : belowFirstCriticalValue μ c)
    (φ : Flow ℝ (LeftEnergyState μ c))
    (hφ : IsLeviCivitaHamiltonianFlow μ c φ)
    (b : ℝ) (hb : 0 < b)
    (hgood : ∀ r ∈ Set.Ioo 0 b, ∃ x : LeftEnergyState μ c, (x : Phase) = farShootingStart μ c r ∧ ∃ τ : ℝ, IsFarShootingArc φ x τ)
    (hbad : ¬ (∃ x : LeftEnergyState μ c, (x : Phase) = farShootingStart μ c b ∧ ∃ τ : ℝ, IsFarShootingArc φ x τ)) :
    ∃ E : ℝ × ℝ,
      (((E.1 = -1 ∨ E.1 = 1) ∧ 0 < E.2) ∨ (E.2 = 0 ∧ Real.sqrt 2 / 2 < E.1)) ∧
      ∀ η > 0, ∃ δ > 0, ∀ r ∈ Set.Ioo (b - δ) b, ∀ x : LeftEnergyState μ c, ∀ τ : ℝ,
        (x : Phase) = farShootingStart μ c r → IsFarShootingArc φ x τ →
          dist (shootingCoordinates μ ((φ τ x : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase)) E < η := by sorry

end BirkhoffGlobalSection
